/*
  RouteTransition.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0192 · RouteTransition (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source (components/motion/
  RouteTransition.tsx) renders NO translatable copy: it is a structural motion wrapper that cross-fades
  its `children` on a route change and reads only two hooks (`useLocation`, `useMotionPreference`). It
  emits no text, no labels, and makes no `t(...)` calls. There are therefore no message keys to mirror —
  this catalog is intentionally free of copy keys, and the Swift sources hold no English literals.

  The surface is also free of interactive elements of its own (it wraps the routed body, which carries
  its own accessibility), and it adds no accessibility semantics over that body, so there is no native
  VoiceOver label / action / hint to localize either. Its one accessibility-relevant behaviour — honour
  Reduce Motion by collapsing the fade to an instant swap — is structural, not textual, and is exercised
  by the decision tests rather than by a string.

  The per-surface table name ("RouteTransition") is reserved here so the file-set stays consistent with
  its sibling surfaces and folds into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time
  should localizable chrome ever be added.
*/
